  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Carranza y Ruiz Arquitectura, Pueblo Serena, Monterrey, with the Sierra Madre behind): a shopping centre laid out like a village round a church, not a mall. The church is a white, plain nave with a row of pointed gables and a tall slim white bell tower (the first, fifth and sixth photographs); around the plaza are two- to four-storey buildings of stacked dark local stone in tall piers with dark metal and perforated-screen infill, deep dark-metal canopies with timber soffits on slanted steel struts, fountains and a channel of water over rock, and a corner block whose perforated metal skin is cut in a leaf pattern with green, yellow and violet panels. Mexican oaks and plane-like trees grow right through the plaza and an oval hole in one canopy lets a tree through. Modelled: the church, its gables and tower, the east range of stone piers under a dark canopy, the south range, the corner block with its patterned screen, the water channel and fountain, the plaza trees. Guessed: the layout (no plan; the photographs show pieces), every dimension, how the buildings join. A public shopping centre placed at its own spot (OpenStreetMap, the retail area Pueblo Serena, via Nominatim); the models's frame is free, not yet fitted to the map."
